    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51350" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Volusĭus</span></b> , i,
		m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
				name of a Roman</i> gens. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> M. Volusius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 16, 12</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Volusius, <i>an old poet</i>, <i>who wrote</i>
			Annales, <i><span class="en">Cat. 36, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">95,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			Volusius Maecianus, <i>a celebrated lawyer</i>, <i>the tutor of Marcus Antoninus</i>, Jul. Capit. in
			Ant. Pio, 12 al.</div>
